{"title":"2011 CEMC Galois Problems/Problem 1a","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_1\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_CEMC_Galois_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2011 CEMC Galois Problems/Problem 1\">Problem 1</a></span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_CEMC_Galois_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=T-1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Jackson gave the following rule to create sequences:\n</p><p>“If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> is a term in your sequence, then the next term in your sequence is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/8/108aaad0bae63c3a986ab6568ba9b95074e7bd2a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{1 - x}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"48\" height=\"40\" />.”\n</p><p>For example, Mary starts her sequence with the number <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>The second term of her sequence is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/7/a47d19968751c75fcbc5e9be783dc8754a7b2c40.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{1 - 3} = \\frac{1}{-2} = -\\frac{1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"149\" height=\"40\" />. Her sequence is now <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/7/a7748d3d38355a68b51bddc29d7647230728287e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-\\frac{1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"29\" height=\"38\" />.\n</p><p>The third term of her sequence is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/9/5f9a38e55a97224222003a38433270691d6410b5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{1 - (-\\frac{1}{2})} = \\frac{1}{1 + \\frac{1}{2}} = \\frac{1}{\\frac{3}{2}} = \\frac{2}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -20px\" width=\"222\" height=\"45\" />. Her sequence is now <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/7/a7748d3d38355a68b51bddc29d7647230728287e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-\\frac{1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"29\" height=\"38\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/4/7547747b133453d3c209cff6cfbf129aa67a6947.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{2}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>The fourth term of her sequence is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/3/4/8347935932629bd281ffac3edf01c8b8069ab1b6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{1 - \\frac{2}{3}} = \\frac{1}{\\frac{1}{3}} = 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -20px\" width=\"120\" height=\"45\" />. Her sequence is now <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/7/a7748d3d38355a68b51bddc29d7647230728287e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-\\frac{1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"29\" height=\"38\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/4/7547747b133453d3c209cff6cfbf129aa67a6947.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{2}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p>Fabien starts his sequence with the number <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, and continues using Jackson’s rule until the sequence has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/e/efe8f67ac18da14c8aa767b8131b0650ac9b9720.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2011$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"35\" height=\"13\" /> terms.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_CEMC_Galois_Problems/Problem_1a&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>What is the second term of his sequence?\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_CEMC_Galois_Problems/Problem_1a&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>From the rule, the second term of the sequence would be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/0/840b18ed8d066db5b86b59db78e702ed2d56949f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{1 - 2} = \\frac{1}{-1} = \\boxed{-1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"156\" height=\"40\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017224843\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.013 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.029 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 64/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1132/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 3392/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   20.448      1 2011_CEMC_Galois_Problems/Problem_1\n100.00%   20.448      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:35645:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017224843 and revision id 278101. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}